From a23ba3c657bcbcad794b6c0bf1a68d6938e200f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:03:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(3d): enable 3D Finish verify gate and fix exposed gouges

Remove ungenerated pocket op R1 and tool EM-0600-4FL from the
shared_face_bodies_finish fixture so verify runs across all six Z-bands
of sample_ap214.step. Add explicit asserts that gate.skipped and
gate.not_judged are absent, zero gouges occur, gate.ok is true, and
S1 records its true shank_hit finding on 118 mm stock.

Fix three 3D finishing bugs exposed by active verify coverage:
- Sample shallow-edge ellipse chords using exact cos_min^3 curvature
  (MAX_CHORD = 0.006 mm) and exact theta = 0 slice crossings in scan.rs.
- Trim 3-axis ring and steep-shallow runs against overhead canopies and
  tight wall V-notches in rings_overhang.rs while keeping 5-axis swarf
  under-equator rings untrimmed.
- Cap raster_pass_spaced eps_chord at 0.005 mm (half DEV_TOL) so off-center
  convex ridge chords stay within simulation tolerance.

Record the design choices in docs/decisions/1840-finish-verify-gate.md.

Changelog: Fix 3D Finish shallow-edge, overhang-trim, and convex-chord gouges and run verify across all sample Z-bands
Effort: max

Fixes #1840
